# Piece Studio — modular feature

Piece Studio lives in `src/features/piece-studio/`. The App Router page is a thin shell.

## Isolation

- Do not import Scale Studio session, progress, detection, or take-history modules.
- Do not reuse Scale Studio localStorage keys. Use `musai-piece-*` only.
- Shared UI (`StudioViewport`, `PracticeHubBackLink`, `MusaiMicCapturePanel`, `MusaiCaptureDock`) is fine. Shared *domain* is not.
- OpenSheetMusicDisplay stays behind `score/ScoreRenderer` → `OpenSheetMusicDisplayRenderer`. The React shell (`OsmdScoreAdapter`) must not import the OSMD package. Overlay geometry stays in `score/`. Do not import OSMD from catalog, parser, playback timing, or Scale Studio.
- MusicXML/MXL remains the structured interchange for engraving. Domain logic (playback, practise, feedback) consumes `MusaiScoreV1`, not raw MusicXML or a renderer SDK.
- Playback timing comes from the MusAI score (`playback/`). OSMD only supplies note positions for the cursor.
- Practise **recording chrome** is the shared `MusaiMicCapturePanel` (`.musai-rec-bar`). Idle bar is mic + record; the tape appears while recording. `PiecePractiseDock` only wraps it and adds Piece **Last take** replay (hidden audio + playhead). Do not restyle mic, record button, or waveform inside Piece CSS — change the shared panel instead. Do not use a native `<audio controls>` widget for take playback.
- Take orchestration lives in `practice/` (`analyzePieceTake`). Skill analyzers live in `feedback/analyzers/`. Shared pitch matching lives in `pitch/`. Score-derived expected notes live in `score/expectedNotes`.
- Unimplemented skills return `not_ready` with no events — do not invent rhythm, tempo, dynamics, or consistency.
- Orchestration is `runPieceFeedback` only — do not put multi-skill DSP in one giant service.
- Coach Parsa consumes `PieceFeedbackReportV1` / `PieceCoachContextV1` from `feedback/`. Do not pass pitch frames, recorders, or Scale Studio sessions into piece coaching.
- Full reports persist in IndexedDB (`feedback` store). Catalog attempts may keep a compact `feedbackSkills` map only.
- Practise UI must not show “not ready” skill names to students.
- Visual feedback preview lives in `feedback/visual/`. One shared panel (`PieceFeedbackReview`) serves every skill: category selector + score annotations. **Pitch** is visual-first — colour on engraved noteheads only (sharp / flat / missed), matching Scale Studio intonation colour, with a short legend in the panel (no bar washes, no per-note Heard/Try cards). Other skills still list issues. Mock issues are labeled `mock-preview` / Sample and must stay out of analyzers and `buildPieceCoachContext`. Do not show `not_ready` skill names. Ask your coach stays secondary. Do not confuse **Hear this** (written notes) with the Listen tab or Last take replay. Recording status belongs on the shared recorder.
- Sheet-music recognition lives behind `omr/OMRProvider`. Do not import Flat, Audiveris, or any vendor from import, catalog, or UI.
- Audiveris (Java) runs only in `services/omr-worker`. Next.js submits jobs and polls — never spawn Audiveris inside a Vercel/serverless request.
- User-facing copy stays simple (“Upload sheet music”, “Reading your music...”). Do not mention OCR, OMR, MusicXML, or providers in the UI.
- Do not change `ScaleTrebleStaff` / VexFlow 5 scale notation for Piece Studio. Piece scores use OSMD (and its nested VexFlow 1.x), isolated to the adapter.

## Layout

Ready/practice UI should fit one viewport (`StudioViewport`). The piece list may scroll inside the shell. Each imported piece has its own `/practice/piece/[slug]` workspace; Score / Listen / Practise are views of that page, not separate routes.
